query:
Failure type narrowing unioned `TypeIs`

### Summary

This is the most trivial form of set-theoretic typing trimmed out of one of my codebases. This did _not_ report on `v0.0.56`, and does on `v0.0.74`.

```py
from typing import Any, Never, Union
import pandas as pd
import pyspark.pandas as ps
from typing_extensions import TypeIs

PandasTypeFrame = Union[ps.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame]
AnyOtherType = Never

class _FrameIdentities():
    """
    A collection of static methods to provide
    identity transformations and checks on DataFrames
    of various provenances.
    """

    @staticmethod
    def isCorePandasFrame(frame:Any) -> TypeIs[pd.DataFrame]:
        """
        A syntactic sugar type guard for a core pandas frame
        """
        return isinstance(frame, pd.DataFrame)

    @staticmethod
    def isPandasOnSparkFrame(frame:Any) -> TypeIs[ps.DataFrame]:
        """
        A syntactic sugar type guard for a pandas-on-spark frame
        """
        return isinstance(frame, ps.DataFrame)

    @classmethod
    def isPandasTypeFrame(cls, frame:Any) -> TypeIs[PandasTypeFrame]:
        """
        A type guard for either flavor of pandas frame
        """
        return cls.isCorePandasFrame(frame) or cls.isPandasOnSparkFrame(frame)

    @classmethod
    def pdFrame(cls, frame:Any) -> pd.DataFrame:
        # Snipped irrelevant frame-casting magic
        return pd.DataFrame([{"foo": 1, "bar": 2}])

def returnsPandas(_df:Union[AnyOtherType, PandasTypeFrame]) -> pd.DataFrame:
    if _FrameIdentities.isPandasTypeFrame(_df):
        if _FrameIdentities.isPandasOnSparkFrame(_df):
            # Coerce
            _df = _FrameIdentities.pdFrame(_df)
        # element `pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown] & ~pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown]` of union `(pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown] & ~pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown]) | pandas.core.frame.DataFrame` is not assignable to `pandas.core.frame.DataFrame` ty(invalid-return-type) // 0.0.74
        return _df
    raise NotImplementedError("Other irrelevant code here")
```

The first `isPandasTypeFrame` guarantees a trivial union of two classes, and the assignment guarded by `.isPandasOnSparkFrame()` guarantees the removal of one of the two classes. The report even makes it clear: `pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown] & ~pyspark.pandas.frame.DataFrame[Unknown]` is `Never`

`Never|Something` is always `Something`.

If the argument is being made that unknown and unknown don't anti-intersect (a bad argument, IMO, and presumes the generic `TypeIs` deserves "unknown" instead of "Any" -- non-specialization is "everything" not "some poorly defined specific thing that may not be the same") -- specializing the `.isPandasOnSparkFrame()` to `TypeIs[ps.DataFrame[Any]]` _still_ reports an error -- and surely `ps.DataFrame[Any]` is a superset of `ps.DataFrame[Unknown]` and _absolutely_ should reduce to `Never`

